# Advance Payment (Token) Module — Final Implementation Plan

## Overview

Track **advance payments (tokens)** to local suppliers. Money-tracking only — integrated with **Accounts**, **Transactions**, and **Daily Cash**. No inventory/product integration.

---

## Lifecycle Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Create Advance Payment"] --> B["💰 Money deducted from Account"]
    B --> C["📝 Auto expense transaction created"]
    C --> D["⏳ Status: Pending"]
    D --> E{"Outcome?"}
    E -->|"Goods Received"| F["✅ Settled — no money moves"]
    E -->|"Deal Cancelled"| G["🔄 Refund — full or partial"]
    E -->|"Partial delivery"| H["📊 Partial refund, then settle"]
    G --> I["💰 Money returned to any account"]
    I --> J["📝 Auto income transaction created"]
    H --> I
```

---

## Data Model

#### [NEW] [advancePayment.model.js](file:///d:/Client%20Projects/Fortunate%20Business%20Management/fortunate-business-management-backend/models/advancePayment.model.js)

```javascript
{
  advanceId: String,              // Auto-generated: "ADV-0001"
  supplierName: String,           // Free text
  supplierPhone: String,          // Optional
  purpose: String,                // What the advance is for

  amount: Number,                 // Original advance amount
  accountId: ObjectId → Account,  // Payment source account
  paymentMethod: "Cash | Bank | Mobile Banking",
  date: Date,                     // When advance was given

  status: "Pending | Settled | Refunded | Partially Settled",
  settledDate: Date,              // When settled/closed

  // Refund history — supports multiple partial refunds to any account
  refunds: [{
    amount: Number,
    date: Date,
    accountId: ObjectId → Account,      // Can differ from original
    paymentMethod: String,
    transactionId: ObjectId → Transaction,
    note: String
  }],

  transactionId: ObjectId → Transaction,  // The original expense transaction

  notes: String,
  isDeleted, createdBy, modifiedBy, deletedBy, timestamps
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `refundedAmount` is **computed** as `sum(refunds[].amount)`, not stored. `remainingAmount = amount - refundedAmount`.

---

## Deletion & Restoration Logic

> [!IMPORTANT]
> User-specified behavior — differs from other modules.

### Deletion (same-day only)

Advance payments can **only be deleted on the same day** they were created (while that day's daily cash session is still open).

| Step | What Happens |
|------|-------------|
| 1 | Validate: advance's date matches today AND today's daily cash is "Open" |
| 2 | **Hard-delete** the original auto expense transaction (not soft-delete, not trash — gone) |
| 3 | **Hard-delete** all refund income transactions (if any partial refunds exist) |
| 4 | **Reverse all balance changes**: return `amount` to original account, deduct each `refund.amount` from its respective account |
| 5 | **Soft-delete** the advance payment record (`isDeleted = true`) → goes to **Trash** |
| 6 | Audit log the deletion |

> No counter/reversal transactions are created. The transactions are simply removed as if they never existed.

### Restoration from Trash

| Step | What Happens |
|------|-------------|
| 1 | Validate: today's daily cash is "Open", original account has sufficient balance |
| 2 | Restore advance payment (`isDeleted = false`) |
| 3 | **Re-create** the original expense transaction (deduct from account) |
| 4 | **Re-create** all refund income transactions (credit to respective accounts) |
| 5 | Audit log the restoration |

> Transactions are auto-recreated fresh — they are never put in the trash bin themselves.

### Non-same-day advances

If the advance was created on a previous day and that day's cash is closed, the advance **cannot be deleted**. The user must use the Settle or Refund workflows instead.

